# Git LFS is scoped to the published v1.0 battery, and nothing else.
#
# Those 16 files are ~1.1 GB and are the paper's released data, so they belong in
# LFS. Everything else tracked as CSV in this repo is something we generate --
# label sets, trace frames, worksheets, pilot samples -- and comes to 1.2 MB in
# total. Keeping that in LFS bought nothing and cost a great deal: on any machine
# without git-lfs installed the clean filter never runs, so those files sit in the
# working tree as real content while HEAD holds a pointer, and `git status` shows
# 66 files permanently "modified". Plain text also means label changes diff in
# review, which is the whole point of committing them.
ADeLe_battery_data/**/*.csv filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# The tiny synthetic test fixture is a plain CSV so the test suite runs on a
# fresh clone without needing Git LFS / an LFS budget.
tests/fixtures/mini_battery.csv text
